# Line endings, decided here rather than by each machine's git.
#
# Two Windows-only CI failures came from this and neither was about Windows.
# `catalog.test.mjs` lifts a function out of `app.mjs` by source and looks for
# `\n}\n`, which a CRLF checkout does not contain: the slice comes back empty
# and the failure reads «filasDeParametros is not defined», naming the function
# and meaning the line endings. The parity page check compares a file rendered
# with `\n` against the one on disk, and reported a diff in which every line
# was identical. Both passed on Linux, which is the worst shape a failure can
# have — it says "Windows" and means "your checkout".
#
# Measured on a Windows 11 machine, not assumed: a fresh clone gave
# `editor/src/app.mjs` with 3588 CRLF endings and the test failed; with this
# file in place and the tree re-checked-out it has none and the test passes
# unchanged. Git Bash, for its part, runs a CRLF shell script without
# complaining — that was checked too, and is not a reason for this.
#
# Nothing here needs CRLF: the editors this repo is written with all read LF,
# and PowerShell has since 5.1.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text, and must not be touched. The `.wasm` ones are test fixtures —
# a component whose signature does not match, one that traps, and a file that
# is not a component at all — and a byte changed in any of them is a test that
# passes for the wrong reason.
*.wasm  binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff2 binary
